s HTTP result was redacted. The provider-wide restart protocol was otherwise strong: healthy pre-restart service and data, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot ID independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, listener, authentication, documents, and DAV lock operation were captured.","limitations":["The HTTP status values for tokenless and token-bearing PUT operations in both lock tests were redacted. Final content and successful LOCK/UNLOCK support lock operation but do not directly prove that the intervening tokenless update was rejected.","Post-restart evidence rehashed budget.csv but only listed brief.txt; brief.txt's original hash was directly verified earlier, and subsequent mutation tests targeted separate temporary files.","The lifecycle snapshots independently confirm the boot-ID transition, service listener, package health, and lack of failed services, but they do not probe WebDAV semantics."]}
